 decision/leftover-socket-file-kept · Leftover socket file is not removed — A killed wrapper's socket file stays in the per-user directory until a next bind of that name takes it over; nothing removes it. · why: by choice: a harmless file in a 0700 directory
+decision/live-rig-hb-arm-keeps-attributes-only · Live rig's HB arm keeps cell attributes and counts only — The live rig's HB arm types one x and one DEL into a fresh box in its own unwrapped pty before any send, and records only cell attributes and counts, never screen text.
 decision/live-round-rig-keys-own-pty · Live-round rig keys only into its own pty — The founder's word anew per chunk binds only the live rig's closed argv grant: at most two down-arrows and Enter only on a read trust row, one x and one DEL in a ready box. Its stop, Ctrl-C into its own pty or a no-key group kill, needs no word; other keys write nothing; viola types into no dialog. · why: A boundary widening bounded as the founder bounded it; a rig is no viola, so the product's own pty seam stays unchanged.
@@ -271,3 +272,3 @@
 decision/stop-background-tasks-count-only · Stop background tasks carried as a count only — Stop's background_tasks is carried only as its length, no element read; null when absent, null or not an array, and a non-array also writes a drift entry. · why: Ratified with the option-text widening.
-decision/stop-session-crons-count-only · Stop session crons carried as a count only — Stop's session_crons is carried only as its length, scheduled_wakes on turn-ended, no element read or kept; null when absent, null or not an array, a non-array also writing one drift entry to the diagnostics detail file; null on an API-error turn end. · why: Ratified as a boundary widening: one number crosses beside the background-task count, no content. · guard: hook_a_stop_holding_scheduled_wakes_carries_their_count_and_no_content
+decision/stop-session-crons-count-only · Stop session crons carried as a count only — Stop's session_crons is carried only as its length, scheduled_wakes on turn-ended, which the wheel rule also reads; no element is read or kept; null when absent, null or not an array, a non-array also writing one drift entry to the diagnostics detail file; null on an API-error turn end. · why: Ratified as a boundary widening: one number crosses beside the background-task count, no content. · guard: hook_a_stop_holding_scheduled_wakes_carries_their_count_and_no_content
 decision/terminal-colour-facts · Terminal colour facts read for list only — NO_COLOR, TERM and COLORTERM are read only by viola list's human mode, only compared, never echoed, logged or set, and decide only whether and how deep SGR is written around already escaped rows. · why: Ratified.
@@ -358,4 +359,5 @@
 decision/live-rig-context-arm-keeps-no-transcript · Live rig's context arm keeps no transcript byte — The live rig's CX arm reads the session transcript through MAX_FRAME, counting only tags past the kept length and keeping no byte of it, and sends only through viola send under the rig's private config.
-decision/live-rig-kept-stamp-owner-only · Live rig's kept stamp owner-only, seeded to its own home — The live rig keeps a stamp from its CS scratch home owner-only and no-clobber, and seeds it only into its own CC scratch home; CC with no kept stamp refuses before its ledger line and before any scratch.
